# Fixed schema ids for es-trade-tools-service (TICK-TRADE-TOOLS, 15 closed record types, D-R14.1). FINAL: options-edge-processing docs/ta-books/catalog/SCHEMA-ID-MAP.md (contracts 0.31.0).
# The service never registers (BrokerGuard.preflightRegistry uses getId) and refuses to start unless every subject below is registered with a schema equal
# to its embedded copy, and TT_ENABLED=false builds nothing, so registration is needed before the FIRST enabled start, not before the held deploy.
# File column: relative to the contracts checkout's `schemas-registry/ta` directory (SCHEMAS_DIR).
# TICK-TRADE-TOOLS revision 21 (contracts 0.33.0): thirteen subjects have TWO versions. Version 1 is the file under schemas-registry/ta/v1 (the id registered before
# revision 21 on dev and production), version 2 the file under schemas-registry/ta with a NEW fixed id = the version-1 id + 20 (2321-2332, 2335): a version of a subject cannot reuse
# the id of a different schema. The fourth column is the registry version. On a registry that already holds version 1 (dev, production) only the version-2 rows import;
# on a registry that never saw the family both do, in this order. TtCheckpointManifest/Chunk are unchanged (one version).
# Version-2 rows after all version-1 rows so the preflight pass can see the predecessor of every row.
